>> title: Creamed Corn
>> category: Vegetables & Sides
>> tags: corn, butter, southern, skillet, side
>> counters: Meat and Three
>> aka: fried corn, skillet corn, cream style corn, corn off the cob
>> servings: 6
>> time: 40 min
>> pairs-with: fried-chicken, stewed-squash, skillet-cornbread
>> step.1: Cut the kernels off, then scrape the bare cobs with the back of the knife. That white liquid is the cream.
>> step.2: cut and scrape the cobs
>> step.3: whisk the slurry
>> step.4: fry in the fat 8 min
>> step.5: stir the slurry through, simmer 8 min

Cut the kernels off and then scrape the bare cobs with the back of the knife. The white liquid that comes off is the cream in creamed corn, and a recipe that opens a carton instead is making a different thing.

Cut @fresh corn{8%ears}(kernels off, cobs scraped for their milk) into a bowl.

Whisk @whole milk{1/2%cup}(120 mL), @all-purpose flour{1%Tbs}(8 g), @granulated sugar{1%tsp} smooth.

Melt @unsalted butter{4%Tbs}(55 g), @bacon fat{1%Tbs}(14 g) in a #cast-iron skillet{} with @&(~2)corn and its milk{} and cook it for ~fry{8%min}.

Stir @&(~2)milk slurry{} into @&(~1)skillet corn{} with @kosher salt{1%tsp}, @black pepper{1/2%tsp} and ~simmer{8%min}.

It thickens again as it stands so it should leave the pan looser than you want it. A splash of water loosens it.
